<onlyinclude>The '''sociology of knowledge''' studies how social institutions, relationships, historical circumstances and practices shape what people accept, produce and transmit as knowledge.

== Explanation ==
A scientific laboratory, religious community and court may use different procedures for deciding what counts as evidence. Sociologists examine how those procedures arise and how authority is organized. Explaining why a community believes a claim is different from proving or disproving the claim.

